From f676cff428d9cc44378afdb0d2c87cf0556b5be5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baverrr <342259467+baverrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:38:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] RavenOS: Add reminders, a sleep screen and a
 voice-controlled alarm

Add three skills, English only for now, sharing one alert system:

- Reminders: "remind me to call mom tomorrow at six", "what are my
  reminders", "cancel my reminder to call mom". When due, a full-screen
  card plays a chime and reads the reminder aloud a few times.
- Sleep: "go to sleep until six thirty" dims the screen to a faint clock
  at the lowest brightness and sets a wake-up alarm; it asks for a time
  if none was given. "Wake me up at seven" only sets the alarm, and
  "wake up" leaves the sleep screen and turns the alarm off.
- Alert control: "turn off" and "snooze (for ten minutes)" for a ringing
  alarm or reminder.

Alerts are stored in shared preferences, scheduled with setAlarmClock,
and scheduled again after a reboot or update. The alarm sound plays in
bursts and pauses for a few seconds after the wake word, so the
microphone can hear the command over it. As a privileged system app
(START_ACTIVITIES_FROM_BACKGROUND) Dicio opens the alert screen directly;
otherwise it falls back to a full-screen notification.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
